/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\\
  Ethanol(1)/water(2) VLE at 101.325 kPa -- MEASURED x, T AND y (the vapour
  composition), so a thermodynamic-consistency test (Gibbs-Duhem) can actually
  run.  Representative literature compilation (textbook 1-atm ethanol-water
  T-x-y; azeotrope near x1 = 0.894).  Pure endpoints omitted (gamma is 0/0 there;
  gamma^inf is taken from the dilute points).

  Self-describing format (units MANDATORY):  columns ( {name;unit;role} ) + grid.
\\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

